{"reference":"Ezekiel 28","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":28,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Tyre and the imagery of verses 1–19","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter speaks directly to the prince and king of Tyre. Its judgment is expressed through lament, garden, precious-stone, and cherub imagery. Because the chapter does not explicitly name Satan, the meaning of this imagery is disputed; it appears within Ezekiel 26–28's address to historical Tyre and its rulers.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 28:1-19"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_028_e4bf499793a6b83852fe7c1c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}